ns but  the Trump campaign has refused even that  basic step we're gonna be in Oklahoma  and it's a crowd like I guess nobody's  seen before in an interview with The  Wall Street Journal the president  admitted some of his supporters might  catch the virus but said it's a very  small percentage let me be clear  anyone planning to attend a large-scale  gathering will face an increased risk of  becoming infected with Koba 19 that  hasn't swayed the campaign the president  has been anxious to return to his  rallies and he's unlikely to back down a  second time after the criticism he faced  for originally scheduling his event in  Tulsa site of the worst race Massacre in  American history on Juneteenth a day  marking the end of slavery  Jaxson cross go Global News Washington  still ahead their lips are sealed but  they have the ticket to fun in Japan  Malala yousufzai who was targeted by the  Taliban for pursuing an education has  completed her degree at Oxford  University the 22 year old posted these  images of her celebration this morning  she completed a degree in philosophy  politics and economics in 2012 she was  shot while returning home from school in  Pakistan in 2014 she was given the Nobel  Peace Prize today she tweeted I don't  know what's ahead for now it will be  Netflix breeding and sleep well done  theme parks are reopening in Japan as  kovat 19 restrictions ease but there's a  new twist  screaming is not allowed on  rollercoasters and the video you're  about to see shows it can be done these  are the top bosses of Japan's most  popular amusement park appearing more  concerned about their masks slipping and  their hair moving the parks say the  change is to help prevent the spread of  the virus through saliva but for thrill  seekers who just can't help themselves  there are no penalties the wheels on  this bus go up and down up next a legend  gets a lift to the next stop  back when we were allowed to travel  there were places in popular movies that  really